[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2920275057","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106256#issuecomment-2920275057","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106256","id":2920275057,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6uD9xx","user":{"login":"Cykyrios","id":53737317,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNzM3MzE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53737317?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios","html_url":"https://github.com/Cykyrios","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-29T18:46:54Z","updated_at":"2025-05-29T18:46:54Z","body":"From my [previous post](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106256#discussion_r2083436791) and the MRP in #105926, wouldn't it be fair to say that the assumption that the base class documentation should already be generated is wrong? I believe the possible cyclic dependency invalidates that assumption, and to be honest, I think relying on generated documentation at all is not the right way to fill `doc.inherits`, after all we already have the scripts themselves, so why would we bother to even look at generated docs of other classes?\r\nWouldn't it be more proper to directly look for the base class' global name, and if that fails use its path? I believe that only if the base class is not valid should we fall back to `get_base_instance_class()`.\r\n\r\nWith that said, I pushed a new version based on the above: we first check the parent script's `local_name` and use that if it's not empty, otherwise we use the parent script's path; if the parent script is not valid, we fall back to `get_base_instance_class()`.\r\nThis works on my 2 affected projects, as well as the MRP, although to be fair, the current master branch also works already for the MRP, maybe something has changed since last time?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2920275057/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3026537425","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106256#issuecomment-3026537425","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106256","id":3026537425,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc60ZUvR","user":{"login":"Cykyrios","id":53737317,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNzM3MzE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53737317?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios","html_url":"https://github.com/Cykyrios","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-02T05:48:31Z","updated_at":"2025-07-02T05:48:31Z","body":"Rebased, if there's still a chance for this to be merged in 4.5, I would appreciate another review (hoping the approach is correct).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3026537425/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3300235975","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106256#issuecomment-3300235975","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106256","id":3300235975,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7EtZrH","user":{"login":"Cykyrios","id":53737317,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNzM3MzE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53737317?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios","html_url":"https://github.com/Cykyrios","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-16T20:23:45Z","updated_at":"2025-09-16T20:23:45Z","body":"Rebased, the reasoning posted at the end of May above is still relevant here.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3300235975/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4093526403","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106256#issuecomment-4093526403","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106256","id":4093526403,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7z_kGD","user":{"login":"Cykyrios","id":53737317,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNzM3MzE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53737317?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios","html_url":"https://github.com/Cykyrios","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-19T21:52:16Z","updated_at":"2026-03-19T21:52:16Z","body":"Could I please get a new review on this? It's been some time and both 4.5 and 4.6 got released in the meantime, but I'm still having the original issue without this fix applied.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4093526403/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4443727611","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106256#issuecomment-4443727611","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106256","id":4443727611,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCN3m-w","user":{"login":"Cykyrios","id":53737317,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNzM3MzE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53737317?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios","html_url":"https://github.com/Cykyrios","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-13T17:37:57Z","updated_at":"2026-05-13T17:37:57Z","body":"I will again ask for a new review if possible, because I am again facing this issue, this time as I generate documentation from the XML files, saved the data in a dictionary, and include it in PCK files for a modular app. I now have a situation where a module's documentation fails to generate because I check whether the documented object inherits from a specific class, and I'm getting the wrong result (MarginContainer instead of my custom class).\r\n\r\nThis time I can't really work around the issue with a custom build, or I would need to distribute that custom build to my users as well, so I would need to compile Godot in CI (I'm generating builds from official Godot templates, and just using a custom build with this PR for my documentation generator).\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nclass_name ModuleLog\r\nextends GISModule  # GISModule inherits from MarginContainer\r\n```\r\n<img width=\"280\" height=\"60\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/391d21bc-8b13-481e-851c-4b4dd20852fe\" />","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4443727611/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4700899499","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106256#issuecomment-4700899499","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106256","id":4700899499,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABGDIIqw","user":{"login":"Cykyrios","id":53737317,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzNzM3MzE3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53737317?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios","html_url":"https://github.com/Cykyrios","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Cykyrios/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-14T06:16:39Z","updated_at":"2026-06-14T06:16:39Z","body":"I'm going to close this as it's indeed an incorrect fix (although it *does* fix all my affected projects).\r\n\r\nThe core issue remains that scripts can fail to get the correct inheritance tree, in both the editor help and XML files generated by `--doctool --gdscript-docs`, depending on the order in which scripts are loaded (which can be different between the editor and doctool, especially when passing a specific folder as argument to doctool).\r\n\r\nI think the problem stems from the dependency resolution when loading scripts, as I detailed [in the linked issue](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105926#issuecomment-4466364409): if script A appears as a dependency in other scripts, then down the dependency chain for A we get script B, which itself depends on A, B's documentation gets generated even though A is not available yet. Usually, if B depends on A, the dependency chain for A would get resolved, A would get generated, and then B would be generated, but since here A is already in the \"dependency wait list\", B gets generated without having all its dependencies satisfied.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4700899499/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]